/**
 * Computes the covariance matrix of the estimated parameters.
 *
 * <p>The covariance matrix is calculated as the inverse of the normal matrix (J^T J),
 * where J is the Jacobian matrix of the residuals with respect to the parameters.
 * This matrix provides insights into the uncertainty and correlation between the
 * estimated parameters, assuming uncorrelated measurement errors with unit variance.
 *
 * <p>Before computing the covariance matrix, the {@code updateJacobian()} method is
 * invoked to ensure the Jacobian matrix is up-to-date based on the current
 * estimation problem state. The Jacobian is expected to be stored in the
